\f1\fs22 We\'92re terribly sorry about this next bit.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>We must leave Cracker and most of Sarah for a time while we venture into the dangerous woods of back-story. We must cast back to an unplaceable time, the placement of which has defied all out attempts to research it out of its hidey-holes under the squeaky floorboards of our current time.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>We can tell you only what we think we know, as far as we can tell we know it. The exact timing of events, even the question of whether certain historical figures even met, have defeated all our attempts of arranging every little black duck in neat, little black rows. There are anachronisms aplenty, and we\'92re sad to report we never resolved whether Sarah was, in the time of events we\'92ve been narrating, in her late twenties or early two hundreds.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Such is the nature of comically faulty universes, we suspect.
